WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:04.930
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:06.330
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:09.210
We were on The Office together, and we're best friends.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》，而且我们是最好的朋友。

4
00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:13.310
And now we're doing the ultimate Office Lovers podcast just for you.
现在，我们专门为你们制作了这个终极《办公室》粉丝播客。

5
00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:17.830
Each week, we will dive deeper into the world of The Office with exclusive interviews,
每周，我们都会通过独家采访深入探索《办公室》的世界，

6
00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:20.990
behind-the-scenes details, and lots of BFF stories.
分享幕后细节，还有许多我们闺蜜之间的故事。

7
00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:23.030
We're the Office Lady 6.0.
我们是《办公室女士 6.0》。

8
00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:26.300
Hello, everyone.
大家好。

9
00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:28.620
Welcome to Office Lady 6.0.
欢迎来到《办公室女士 6.0》。

10
00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:33.820
Today, we are going back to the very beginning of the world of The Office.
今天，我们要回到《办公室》世界的最初起点。

11
00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:37.400
And we have a special guest to help us travel back in time.
我们请到了一位特别嘉宾，带我们一起穿越回过去。

12
00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:42.540
Angela, that is such a poetic way to describe this episode.
安吉拉，你描述这一集的方式真是太有诗意了。

13
00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:43.140
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

14
00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:44.080
I got here early.
我来早了。

15
00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:45.940
I just had a lot of free time on my hands.
我刚好有很多空闲时间。

16
00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:47.700
Maybe I overthought that one.
也许我刚才想得太多了。

17
00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:49.520
You know, I don't know what got into me.
你知道，我也不知道自己是怎么了。

18
00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:50.600
I love an origin story.
我喜欢起源故事。

19
00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:51.260
What can I say?
我能说什么呢？

20
00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:54.420
Well, it is true that today we are starting at the beginning.
嗯，确实，今天我们要从头开始。

21
00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:58.340
We have re-watched the BBC pilot of The Office.
我们重温了英版《办公室》的试播集。

22
00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:03.340
And as it turns out, I have a connection to someone from the BBC office,
结果发现，我和英版《办公室》里的某个人有联系，

23
00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:04.400
and they're joining us today.
她今天会加入我们。

24
00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:05.560
You do.
你确实有。

25
00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:07.180
Tell them who it is, lady.
告诉大家是谁吧，女士。

26
00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:10.360
My lady friend just texted Lucy Davis because they're pals.
我的这位女士朋友刚刚给露西·戴维斯发了短信，因为她们是好朋友。

27
00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:13.540
Lucy plays Dawn Tinsley in the BBC The Office.
露西在英版《办公室》中饰演道恩·廷斯利。

28
00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:19.160
She's joining us in the studio today to give us all the behind-the-scenes details of how the show began.
她今天会来到演播室，为我们揭秘这部剧最初是如何开始的幕后细节。

29
00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:21.160
Well, you know Lucy from The Office.
嗯，你们通过《办公室》认识了露西。

30
00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:27.300
And she was also in Shaun of the Dead, Wonder Woman, and Chilling Adventures of Sabrina.
她还出演过《僵尸肖恩》、《神奇女侠》和《萨布丽娜的惊心冒险》。

31
00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:29.920
She's just the loveliest person and very, very funny.
她真的是个非常可爱、非常幽默的人。

32
00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:32.040
We are so excited to have her here with us.
我们非常高兴她能来到这里。

33
00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:34.280
Lady, she is the original Office lady.
女士，她才是最初的“办公室女士”。

34
00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:35.280
She is.
确实如此。

35
00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:37.360
So I think we should just jump right in.
所以我觉得我们应该直接开始吧。

36
00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:38.160
Here we go.
我们开始吧。

37
00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:43.030
Hello.
你好。

38
00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:47.100
And guest here today, Lucy.
今天的嘉宾，露西。

39
00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:47.880
Hello.
你好。

40
00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:51.360
It is Lucy Davis, you guys.
伙计们，是露西·戴维斯。

41
00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:53.020
Dawn Tinsley.
道恩·廷斯利。

42
00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:53.400
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

43
00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:53.720
Dawn.
道恩。

44
00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:55.700
From The Original Office.
来自最初的《办公室》。

45
00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:58.840
The UK version of The Office.
英版《办公室》。

46
00:01:58.940 --> 00:01:59.320
The OG.
鼻祖。

47
00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:01.660
Why we ever had jobs in the first place.
我们当初能有工作全靠它。

48
00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:03.540
Oh, I'm glad this is down to me.
哦，很高兴这事儿落到我头上了。

49
00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:04.920
Okay, good, good.
好的，很好，很好。

50
00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:05.440
Thank you.
谢谢。

51
00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:07.480
We can leave Rick and Steve way out of this.
我们可以把瑞克和史蒂夫排除在外。

52
00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:09.600
Well, they're not here today.
好吧，他们今天没来。

53
00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:10.160
They're not here.
他们没在这儿。

54
00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:11.220
So there we are.
所以情况就是这样。

55
00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:11.660
There you go.
就是这样。

56
00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:12.560
The show is mine.
这节目现在归我了。

57
00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:13.180
That's right.
没错。

58
00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:13.900
That's right.
没错。

59
00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:17.960
You know, we're so excited to have you on today.
你知道，我们很高兴你能来参加今天的节目。

60
00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:23.320
We're going to break down the pilot episode of the BBC's The Office.
我们将深入剖析BBC版《办公室》的试播集。

61
00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:23.860
Yeah.
没错。

62
00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:25.280
You're going to take us through it.
你将带我们一起回顾。

63
00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:26.640
We're going to ask you questions.
我们会向你提问。

64
00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:27.080
Yeah.
好的。

65
00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:28.360
It's pretty cool.
这真的很酷。

66
00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:31.480
But, you know, we always like to kick things off by asking people,
但是，你知道，我们总是喜欢以一个问题作为开场，

67
00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:33.620
how did you get your job on The Office?
你是怎么得到《办公室》这份工作的？

68
00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:39.120
Oh, I tell you when it was 1999 and it was just everyone was breaking up for Christmas
噢，我告诉你，那是1999年，当时大家都准备放圣诞假了，

69
00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:45.040
and I had auditioned for a bunch of comedy pilots, none of which I had particularly gelled with.
我试镜了一堆喜剧试播集，但没觉得哪个特别适合我。

70
00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:51.620
It was still in a time when those, you know, live audience comedies were very, very broad
那时候，那种有现场观众的喜剧风格还非常非常夸张，

71
00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:52.860
and nothing against that.
我并不是对那种风格有意见。

72
00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:55.240
I just didn't fit easily into that.
只是我不太适合那种表演。

73
00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:57.300
And so I went in and I auditioned.
所以我去参加了试镜。

74
00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:58.960
Ricky Gervais wasn't there then.
瑞奇·热维斯当时不在场。

75
00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:00.320
And I auditioned.
然后我就参加了试镜。

76
00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:03.560
Then I got a call back and then Ricky was there and Steve Merchant.
后来我接到了回电，瑞奇和史蒂夫·莫昌特都在那儿。

77
00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:08.560
And we were in a tiny room with an extremely large table.
我们在一个极小的房间里，里面放着一张特别大的桌子。

78
00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:11.220
So you had to kind of shimmy your way around it.
所以你得侧着身子挪过去。

79
00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:16.800
And I did a scene, which stayed in the pilot, where Dawn gets fake fired.
我演了一场戏，后来被保留在试播集里了，就是道恩被假装解雇的那场。

80
00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:18.520
That's what I auditioned with.
那就是我试镜时演的内容。

81
00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:20.180
That's what I auditioned with.
那就是我试镜时演的内容。

82
00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:20.880
Oh my.
天哪。

83
00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:21.420
Okay.
好吧。

84
00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:22.740
But that's so funny.
但这太搞笑了。

85
00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:24.120
That was our audition scene.
那就是我们的试镜片段。

86
00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:24.540
Yeah.
是啊。

87
00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:25.440
That's mad.
太疯狂了。

88
00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:25.960
Yeah.
是啊。

89
00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:30.900
And originally, I don't know what was in yours, but in ours, originally,
最初，我不知道你们那版是什么样，但在我们这版里，最初，

90
00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:35.980
when Dawn then is crying and breaking down, Ricky tries to explain it's a joke.
当道恩哭着崩溃时，瑞奇试图解释这只是个玩笑。

91
00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:41.280
She says something to him and walks out the room, but trips and falls.
她对他说了一些话，然后走出房间，却被绊倒了。

92
00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:47.300
So when we were in this audition room, I was thinking, I'm not going to trip and fall
所以当我们在试镜室里时，我在想，我可不要绊倒，

93
00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:52.020
because it just feels so weird and uncomfortable in this room.
因为在这个房间里感觉太奇怪、太不自在了。

94
00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:53.980
Not uncomfortable in the good, uncomfortable way.
不是那种好的、让人不自在的感觉。

95
00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:54.280
Yeah.
是啊。

96
00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:54.660
Right.
没错。

97
00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:55.860
So I didn't.
所以我没演绊倒。

98
00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:00.460
And then at the end of the scene, Ricky kept going as David Brent.
然后在那场戏结束时，瑞奇一直以大卫·布伦特的身份演下去。

99
00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:02.660
And so I kept going.
于是我也一直演下去。

100
00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:06.800
And then after a while, I was like, yeah, I'm probably going to run out of things to say.
过了一会儿，我就想，好吧，我大概快没词儿说了。

101
00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:07.500
So what do I do?
那我该怎么办？

102
00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:08.240
Oh, I know.
哦，我知道了。

103
00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:09.160
I'll just leave the room.
我就直接离开房间。

104
00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:11.600
So I just exited the room and went.
于是我就走出了房间，然后离开了。

105
00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:13.860
And then I just heard Ricky roaring.
接着我就听见瑞奇在咆哮。

106
00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:15.360
I was like, apparently that was okay.
我当时心想，看来那样做没问题。

107
00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:19.580
And then I got it and I was really pleased.
后来我拿到了那个角色，真的非常高兴。

108
00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:22.320
And I had to sign a contract, I think, for six years.
我记得我好像签了一份六年的合同。

109
00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:23.820
And that was very new in England.
这在当时的英国是非常新鲜的事。

110
00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:35.720
And now, of course, I couldn't be more glad to have got this job.
当然，现在我无比庆幸自己得到了这份工作。

111
00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:36.200
Yeah.
是啊。

112
00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:37.400
It was a joy.
那真是一段快乐的时光。

113
00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:42.560
And the fact that no one said, don't forget, this is a funny line, so really make it funny.
而且没有人会特意叮嘱说，别忘了，这句台词很有趣，一定要演得好笑一点。

114
00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:49.320
Don't, you know, and everything had to just be as real as possible was my comfort zone.
不用那样，你知道，一切都要尽可能真实，这正是我感到自在的表演方式。

115
00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:52.380
And my, like, no one had ever asked me to do that before.
而且，以前从来没有人要求我那样做。

116
00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:55.760
It was all like, be a good actor, but it's acting.
以前总是被要求做一个好演员，但那是在“演戏”。

117
00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.840
And now this is just being.
而现在，这只是在“生活”。

118
00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:01.680
You were so good, though, your timing.
不过你演得真好，你的节奏感太棒了。

119
00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:07.320
And when I watched it the first time, you know, years before the U.S.
当我第一次看这部剧时，那是在美版播出前好几年。

120
00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:11.520
version, I really didn't think it was scripted.
我真的以为那不是写好的剧本。

121
00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:21.040
I was one of those people that thought they just, you know, I thought, well, David Brent is a crazy character of a person, but I'd also worked for some really weird bosses.
我当时就是那种人，我以为他们只是……你知道，我心想，大卫·布伦特是个疯狂的角色，但我以前也确实给一些很古怪的老板打过工。

122
00:05:21.640 --> 00:05:23.200
And so I kind of bought it.
所以我当时就信以为真了。

123
00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:28.020
But I thought you were just in the moment.
但我以为你们只是在即兴发挥。

124
00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:28.920
Yeah, we were.
没错，我们确实是。

125
00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:33.060
It was really a joyous freedom.
那真是一种令人愉悦的自由。

126
00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:34.300
I don't know if you felt this.
不知道你是否有同感。

127
00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:39.540
Just to, you know what's happening is also funny, but you just get to be.
就是，你知道发生的这一切本身就很有趣，你只需要沉浸其中。

128
00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:41.160
You just get to be real.
你只需要表现得真实自然。

129
00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:47.960
No one's trying to make a big thing about a joke and making sure you have three laughs a page and all of that kind of stuff.
没有人刻意去制造笑点，也不用确保每页纸都要有三个笑料之类的东西。

130
00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:50.560
And that was a freedom for me.
这对我是种解脱。

131
00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:51.460
I loved it.
我太喜欢了。

132
00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:58.780
The rhythm of it, like what Angela is saying and what you're talking about when I saw it again before I ever even knew I was going to audition.
那种节奏，就像安吉拉所说的，还有你刚才提到的，我在还没听说要试镜之前又看了一遍。

133
00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:01.380
Before I even knew there would be this American version.
在甚至不知道会有美版之前。

134
00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:14.240
I was just completely struck by how funny it was to be off rhythm and to sit in things for awkward amounts of time.
我完全被那种打破常规的节奏感所震撼，还有那种在尴尬时刻停顿的表演。

135
00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:19.780
And it was a new comedic rhythm that you guys just invented together.
那是你们共同创造的一种全新的喜剧节奏。

136
00:06:19.970 --> 00:06:21.000
It was so cool.
太酷了。

137
00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:25.980
There was a show in England that had already started airing called The Royal Family, R-O-Y-L-E.
英国当时有一部已经播出的剧叫《罗伊一家》，拼写是R-O-Y-L-E。

138
00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:29.860
And that was a similar style.
那部剧的风格很相似。

139
00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:34.360
And if you've never seen The Royal Family, please see it.
如果你还没看过《罗伊一家》，请一定要看。

140
00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:37.200
If you guys have never seen it, it's so good.
如果你们还没看过，它真的非常棒。

141
00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:37.980
It's so uncomfortable.
那种感觉非常令人坐立难安。

142
00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:41.320
And it's really just a family on a couch in a living room.
它真的就是一家人坐在客厅的沙发上。

143
00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:43.880
And anyway.
总之。

144
00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:45.440
I can't wait to check it out.
我迫不及待想去看看了。

145
00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:47.360
Yeah, check it out or I'll send you a link.
好啊，去看看吧，或者我发个链接给你。

146
00:06:47.560 --> 00:06:47.720
Yeah.
好。

147
00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:54.380
But yeah, when I watched that, I remember thinking that would be a fun role as an actor to play.
不过确实，看那部剧的时候，我记得当时就在想，作为演员能演那样的角色一定很有趣。

148
00:06:55.780 --> 00:07:05.960
So doing The Office, yeah, ever since then, I did my first multicam a couple of years ago.
所以后来演《办公室》，是的，从那以后，几年前我第一次尝试了多机位拍摄。

149
00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:10.240
And I knew, of course, that the style isn't going to be The Office or whatever.
我当然知道，那种风格不会是《办公室》之类的。

150
00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:20.740
But it was interesting for me and a strange experience to have to make so much of the comedy lines.
但对我来说，必须把那么多喜剧台词演出来，这是一种很有趣且奇特的经历。

151
00:07:21.020 --> 00:07:22.820
I was like, but if they're funny, they're funny.
我当时就想，如果他们本身就很有趣，那他们就是很有趣。

152
00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:25.340
You don't have to add a bell and whistle on it.
你没必要在上面画蛇添足。

153
00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:25.780
Yeah.
是啊。

154
00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:26.400
So, yeah.
所以，没错。

155
00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:28.240
I came from sketch comedy.
我是演小品出身的。

156
00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:28.900
Right.
对。

157
00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:35.860
And so, when I, my first scene, you know, the first, like, few lines I had, I thought, oh, I'm getting fired.
所以当我，拍第一场戏的时候，你知道，我前几句台词，我就想，完了，我要被炒鱿鱼了。

158
00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:37.600
I was doing so much.
我演得太用力了。

159
00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:39.020
But I was because I was doing that.
但我当时就是那样演的。

160
00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:40.640
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊，是啊。

161
00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:42.360
But it is such a different style.
但这确实是完全不同的风格。

162
00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:43.600
You guys did it so well.
你们演得太棒了。

163
00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:44.760
But I have a question.
但我有个问题。

164
00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:49.400
When you were filming the pilot, did you feel like, oh, we've got something here?
当你们在拍试播集的时候，有没有那种感觉，就是，噢，我们拍出好东西了？

165
00:07:49.540 --> 00:07:51.180
Like, this is going to be a hit?
就是，这会火吗？

166
00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:53.060
Because we felt that way.
因为我们当时就有这种感觉。

167
00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:55.540
We didn't know if every—
我们不知道是不是每个人——

168
00:07:55.540 --> 00:07:57.000
I wouldn't say a hit.
我不会说是火。

169
00:07:57.280 --> 00:07:58.180
Well, no, but—
好吧，不，但是——

170
00:07:58.180 --> 00:07:58.920
I thought—
我以为——

171
00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:00.800
I thought we had something special.
我以为我们拍出了特别的东西。

172
00:08:01.140 --> 00:08:01.500
Amazing.
太棒了。

173
00:08:01.820 --> 00:08:03.360
I didn't think anyone was going to watch it.
我没觉得会有人看。

174
00:08:03.380 --> 00:08:04.340
That's how I felt.
我当时也是这种感觉。

175
00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:05.080
Yeah, that's the thing.
对，就是这样。

176
00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:08.020
I was like, if people will watch this, it's going to be a hit.
我当时想，如果人们愿意看这个，它一定会火。

177
00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:09.480
I don't know if they're going to watch it.
但我不知道他们会不会看。

178
00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:11.060
Is that—that was your experience?
那是——那是你的经历吗？

179
00:08:11.060 --> 00:08:12.420
That's how I definitely felt.
我确实是那种感觉。

180
00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:19.620
I just remember really praying that it would go because I loved doing this so much.
我只记得当时真的在祈祷它能成功，因为我太喜欢拍这个了。

181
00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:27.240
And we made—I think I told you this, Jenna, that we actually made a pilot, and then we remade the pilot.
而且我们拍了——我想我跟你说过，珍娜，我们其实拍了一个试播集，然后又重拍了一次。

182
00:08:27.460 --> 00:08:27.780
Yes.
是的。

183
00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:30.440
And the original pilot, there were some different things.
最初的试播集里，有些地方不太一样。

184
00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:40.640
But the biggest difference was there had been this documentary reality show in those very early days called—I think it was called Airline.
但最大的区别在于，在那个早期阶段，有一部纪录片式的真人秀，叫——我想是叫《航空公司》。

185
00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:45.540
And it was just cameras following an airline in a smallish airport in England.
内容就是摄像机跟拍英国一个小机场的航空公司。

186
00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:47.700
And it became huge.
结果它火得一塌糊涂。

187
00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:51.420
And suddenly, like, these people were, like, famous.
突然之间，这些人就变得很有名了。

188
00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:57.460
And there was an actor called John Nettles who narrated the documentary.
而且有一位叫约翰·内特尔斯的演员为那部纪录片做了旁白。

189
00:08:57.820 --> 00:09:01.380
So we had him narrate the pilot.
所以我们也让他为试播集做了旁白。

190
00:09:01.740 --> 00:09:02.100
Oh.
噢。

191
00:09:02.460 --> 00:09:02.540
Yeah.
是啊。

192
00:09:02.900 --> 00:09:06.660
To make it as real, like, kind of this genre and this style.
为了让它看起来更真实，就像那种类型和风格一样。

193
00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:17.340
And—but then I think, I believe—this was such a long time ago now—but I believe they felt that it took time away from story and comedy.
然后——但后来我想，我相信——这已经是好久以前的事了——但我相信他们觉得这占用了故事和喜剧的时间。

194
00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:19.820
So we redid it again and had—
所以我们又重拍了一次，并且让——

195
00:09:19.820 --> 00:09:20.500
Without him.
没有他。

196
00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:21.540
Without the narration.
没有旁白。

197
00:09:21.860 --> 00:09:22.000
Yeah.
是啊。

198
00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:22.320
Yeah.
没错。

199
00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:27.600
And the original theme tune just for that pilot was ELO's Mr. Blue Sky.
而且那个试播集最初的主题曲是ELO乐队的《蓝天先生》。

200
00:09:27.980 --> 00:09:28.240
I remember that.
我记得那个。

201
00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:28.520
What?
什么？

202
00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:30.220
That was our original theme song?
那是我们最初的主题曲吗？

203
00:09:30.220 --> 00:09:30.640
Yes, yes.
是的，是的。

204
00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:30.940
Yes.
没错。

205
00:09:31.220 --> 00:09:32.620
Is that—I never knew that.
是吗——我从来都不知道。

206
00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:32.960
What?
什么？

207
00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:33.500
Did you know that?
你知道吗？

208
00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:34.080
No.
不知道。

209
00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:34.280
No.
不知道。

210
00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:35.440
I'm getting chills.
我起鸡皮疙瘩了。

211
00:09:36.460 --> 00:09:37.620
Did Greg know that?
格雷格知道吗？

212
00:09:37.740 --> 00:09:38.920
I don't know if Greg knew that.
我不知道格雷格知不知道。

213
00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:47.660
But when I—when Greg gave us a screener of the pilot and we all got together and we watched it, the theme song was Mr. Blue Sky.
但当格雷格给我们试播集样片，我们聚在一起看的时候，主题曲是《Mr. Blue Sky》。

214
00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:51.940
You have to ask him if he knew that that—because in ours, obviously, it never got aired.
你得问问他知不知道那件事——因为在我们的版本里，显然那首歌从未播出过。

215
00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:52.780
Yeah, same.
是啊，我也是。

216
00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:53.320
Yeah, yeah.
对，没错。

217
00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:57.940
But we couldn't—Greg told us, oh, we can't use that song because—
但我们没法——格雷格告诉我们，哦，我们不能用那首歌，因为——

218
00:09:57.940 --> 00:09:58.760
Another show—
另一部剧——

219
00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:00.100
Another show nabbed it.
另一部剧抢先用了。

220
00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:04.080
So then he had a friend who composed the song that we ultimately use.
所以他找了个朋友创作了我们最终使用的那首歌。

221
00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:05.360
It's a great song, though.
不过那首歌真的很棒。

222
00:10:05.460 --> 00:10:07.280
Yours is a great song, though, too.
你们那首歌也很棒。

223
00:10:07.600 --> 00:10:07.720
Yeah.
是啊。

224
00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:13.180
Because obviously ours was Stereophonics, and less than this, which is fine.
因为显然我们用的是Stereophonics乐队的歌，虽然没那么出名，但也挺好的。

225
00:10:13.180 --> 00:10:17.340
They didn't give us permission to use their song, Handbanks of Gladrags.
他们没授权给我们用那首歌，《Handbags and Gladrags》。

226
00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:19.280
So it was kind of rewritten to be that.
所以它被改写成了现在的样子。

227
00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:24.880
And then when it got big, they said that we could use it, but we liked ours by that point.
后来剧火了，他们说我们可以用了，但那时候我们已经喜欢上自己的版本了。

228
00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:30.940
And originally, with Mr. Blue Sky, the opening credits weren't images of Slough.
而且最初用《Mr. Blue Sky》的时候，片头画面也不是斯劳的景象。

229
00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:37.020
It was David Brent walking into work all proud and pompous in his suit and his briefcase and stuff.
那是大卫·布伦特穿着西装、提着公文包，一脸自豪又自负地去上班的画面。

230
00:10:37.140 --> 00:10:39.180
So, yeah, it was pretty different.
所以，是的，当时真的很不一样。

231
00:10:39.460 --> 00:10:41.180
I love the opening images.
我喜欢现在的片头画面。

232
00:10:41.520 --> 00:10:42.000
Same.
我也是。

233
00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:44.320
We were in London a few years ago.
几年前我们在伦敦。

234
00:10:44.460 --> 00:10:45.700
We actually crossed paths, Jenna.
我们其实偶遇过，珍娜。

235
00:10:45.780 --> 00:10:46.520
It was so fun.
太有趣了。

236
00:10:47.180 --> 00:10:53.280
But I was on a train with my husband and kids, and I didn't realize that we were going to go through Slough.
当时我和丈夫还有孩子们在火车上，我没意识到我们要经过斯劳。

237
00:10:53.560 --> 00:10:55.360
And so I said to them, we have to get off.
所以我对他们说，我们必须下车。

238
00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:55.880
And they're like, what?
他们问，什么？

239
00:10:55.980 --> 00:10:56.720
This isn't our stop.
这不是我们要下的站。

240
00:10:56.820 --> 00:10:57.200
Oh, that's good.
哦，那太好了。

241
00:10:57.200 --> 00:11:01.000
And we jumped off really fast just so I could get a picture, and then we jumped back on the train.
我们飞快地跳下车，就为了拍张照，然后又跳回了火车上。

242
00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:04.020
Did you post the picture?
你把照片发出来了吗？

243
00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:04.360
I did.
发了。

244
00:11:04.360 --> 00:11:04.780
I did.
我发了。

245
00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:05.660
I had to go look for it.
我得去翻翻看。

246
00:11:06.920 --> 00:11:12.700
So, I remember a story that Stephen Merchant told when they first came to visit the set.
我记得斯蒂芬·莫昌特讲过一个故事，关于他们第一次来片场探班的时候。

247
00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:13.020
Yeah.
嗯。

248
00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:19.360
He said that after the very first episode aired, he was sitting on the train.
他说第一集播出后，他坐在火车上。

249
00:11:19.640 --> 00:11:19.900
Yeah.
嗯。

250
00:11:20.080 --> 00:11:26.500
And he overheard a woman asking her friends if she had seen the documentary about the crazy guy in an office.
他无意中听到一个女人问她的朋友，有没有看过那个关于办公室里疯子的纪录片。

251
00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:27.540
Oh, God.
天哪。

252
00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:31.400
And that the friend said, oh, that's not a real documentary.
然后那个朋友说，哦，那不是真正的纪录片。

253
00:11:31.400 --> 00:11:32.540
That's a comedy show.
那是喜剧节目。

254
00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:36.000
And that the woman said, oh, well, then it isn't very funny.
结果那个女人说，哦，那它一点也不好笑。

255
00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:37.160
Oh, that's great.
哦，那太棒了。

256
00:11:37.720 --> 00:11:43.240
But what was crazy was he said, like, she loved it when she thought it was a documentary.
但最疯狂的是他说，她以为是纪录片时非常喜欢。

257
00:11:43.240 --> 00:11:47.100
And then when she found out it was a comedy show, she was like, oh, no, no, I don't care for it.
可当她发现那是喜剧节目时，她就说，哦，不，我不喜欢。

258
00:11:47.380 --> 00:11:49.980
But what was the reaction when it came out?
那它刚出来时反响如何？

259
00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:50.660
Do you remember?
你还记得吗？

260
00:11:51.760 --> 00:11:53.160
It was slow.
反响很慢。

261
00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:58.220
We were on a network called BBC Two, which tends to have a lot less viewers.
我们在BBC二台播出，那个台的观众通常少得多。

262
00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:06.900
I think Stephen Rickey told me that the pilot got only just a few more viewers than women's
我想斯蒂芬·里基告诉我，试播集的收视率只比女子

263
00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:07.800
Bowls.
草地滚球比赛高一点点。

264
00:12:07.980 --> 00:12:08.280
Yes.
是的。

265
00:12:08.900 --> 00:12:09.760
Bowling or Bowls or something.
保龄球还是草地滚球之类的。

266
00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:10.050
Yes.
是的。

267
00:12:10.740 --> 00:12:18.020
I actually read that it was, in fact, scored one of the lowest ratings in BBC history.
我其实读到过，它确实创下了BBC史上最低的收视率之一。

268
00:12:18.260 --> 00:12:18.500
Yeah.
是啊。

269
00:12:18.680 --> 00:12:19.020
Yeah.
是啊。

270
00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:23.780
But that was the great thing about, I mean, in England, they do this more because, A,
但这就是它的伟大之处，我的意思是，在英国，他们更常这样做，因为第一，

271
00:12:23.860 --> 00:12:26.680
we've only did six episodes as our whole season.
我们整个季度只拍了六集。

272
00:12:26.940 --> 00:12:28.420
So there are already shops.
所以片子都已经做好了。

273
00:12:28.660 --> 00:12:30.340
You may as well air them, I guess.
我想，反正也得播。

274
00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:34.560
And it was BBC Two is not as big a channel as BBC One.
而且BBC二台不像BBC一台那么大的频道。

275
00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:37.720
And so I think it was always just going to air.
所以我认为它本来就注定会播出。

276
00:12:37.880 --> 00:12:39.380
And it just gradually picked up.
然后它就慢慢火起来了。

277
00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:44.800
And over time, a lot of people did say I thought it was a documentary at firSt.
久而久之，很多人确实说，我一开始还以为那是纪录片呢。

278
00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:45.300
Yeah.
是啊。

279
00:12:45.680 --> 00:12:46.380
Did you ever have that?
你有过这种经历吗？

280
00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:48.260
No.
没有。

281
00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:48.780
No.
没有。

282
00:12:48.780 --> 00:12:53.960
I think because we were on, like, NBC, must-see TV.
我想是因为我们在NBC的“必看电视”时段播出。

283
00:12:54.280 --> 00:12:54.580
Right.
没错。

284
00:12:54.740 --> 00:12:54.960
Yeah.
是啊。

285
00:12:55.780 --> 00:12:58.160
And your show had been so popular.
而且你们的剧已经非常受欢迎了。

286
00:12:58.380 --> 00:12:58.660
Right.
没错。

287
00:12:58.660 --> 00:13:00.020
Yeah, that everybody knew.
是啊，大家都知道。

288
00:13:00.140 --> 00:13:05.360
I mean, the big hill that we had to climb was living up to the original.
我的意思是，我们面临的最大挑战就是不辜负原版。

289
00:13:05.780 --> 00:13:12.120
Like, there were so many critics and fans who were, like, sort of, I feel like, actively
当时有很多评论家和粉丝，感觉他们好像在积极地

290
00:13:12.120 --> 00:13:13.720
rooting for us to fail.
盼着我们失败。

291
00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:16.080
Because they didn't want to take anything.
因为他们不想接受任何改变。

292
00:13:16.420 --> 00:13:20.480
They didn't want us to, like, tarnish the reputation of your show.
他们不想让我们玷污你们剧集的声誉。

293
00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:26.120
I will say, there have been times, and certainly back then, where people would say to me back
我得说，确实有过那么几次，尤其是在那个时候，人们会跟我说，

294
00:13:26.120 --> 00:13:29.860
then, as if I would want to hear this, oh, it won't do very well.
好像我很想听似的，哦，它不会成功的。

295
00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:32.360
And I was like, but wouldn't it be great if it did?
我就说，但如果它成功了不是很好吗？

296
00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:36.960
Like, it doesn't affect me one way or the other, what it does.
它成功与否对我来说都没什么影响。

297
00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:38.000
Oh, that's so nice of you.
哦，你真是太好了。

298
00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:39.120
But why would anyone?
但为什么会有人那样呢？

299
00:13:39.320 --> 00:13:43.860
I find it very, it's just strange when anyone wishes some failure on anyone.
我觉得很奇怪，为什么有人会希望别人失败。

300
00:13:43.860 --> 00:13:50.100
I remember getting a pilot once, and I got let go before we even taped it.
我记得有次接了一部试播集，结果还没开始录制我就被解雇了。

301
00:13:50.240 --> 00:13:52.620
And it's very hard to be let go from a pilot.
被试播集淘汰是非常难受的。

302
00:13:52.800 --> 00:13:55.200
But when they got picked up, I couldn't have been more happy.
但当他们被选中时，我真的再高兴不过了。

303
00:13:55.420 --> 00:13:58.920
And I emailed everyone and said, congrats, it's just life.
我给每个人发了邮件，说恭喜，这就是生活。

304
00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:00.720
Just move through it.
继续前行就好。

305
00:14:00.880 --> 00:14:05.640
You don't have to hope that someone fails so that you feel better about yourself.
你没必要为了让自己感觉好受点，而去盼着别人失败。

306
00:14:06.060 --> 00:14:08.360
So it was quite fascinating that.
所以那件事真的很令人着迷。

307
00:14:08.460 --> 00:14:10.860
And I bet you did have that a lot.
我敢说你肯定经常遇到这种情况。

308
00:14:10.860 --> 00:14:16.640
But I will tell you that I've watched every episode of your show through 10, 12 times.
但我得告诉你，你的剧我每一集都看了十到十二遍。

309
00:14:16.760 --> 00:14:17.760
I bet I know it more than you do.
我敢说我比你还了解它。

310
00:14:17.860 --> 00:14:18.180
Really?
真的吗？

311
00:14:18.360 --> 00:14:19.460
That is so wild to me.
这对我来说太不可思议了。

312
