00:46:31.300 --> 00:46:35.760
But it was a wonderful, wonderful little moment of scene.
但那是一个非常、非常美妙的场景片段。

1128
00:46:36.320 --> 00:46:40.220
We shot that same scene for our pilot.
我们为试播集拍过同样的场景。

1129
00:46:40.440 --> 00:46:42.580
That was my other audition scene.
那是我的另一场试镜戏。

1130
00:46:42.580 --> 00:46:47.360
So I had the fake firing scene as my audition scene.
我当时用那场假开除的戏作为试镜片段。

1131
00:46:47.500 --> 00:46:51.000
And then I had this eating lunch scene.
然后还有这场吃午餐的戏。

1132
00:46:51.340 --> 00:46:52.820
But ours got cut.
但我们的被剪掉了。

1133
00:46:53.520 --> 00:46:54.180
I know.
我知道。

1134
00:46:54.340 --> 00:46:55.680
It didn't make it in for time.
因为时长限制没能放进去。

1135
00:46:55.880 --> 00:47:00.000
Because we had to get our episodes down to like 21 minutes, 30 seconds.
因为我们必须把每集压缩到21分30秒左右。

1136
00:47:00.220 --> 00:47:00.580
Oh, that's hot.
哦，那可真够紧凑的。

1137
00:47:00.960 --> 00:47:02.440
So we were like 29.
我们当时拍了29分钟。

1138
00:47:02.520 --> 00:47:04.180
Yeah, you guys had extra time.
是啊，你们有额外的时间。

1139
00:47:04.280 --> 00:47:04.460
Yeah.
没错。

1140
00:47:05.100 --> 00:47:13.020
But this sort of like physicality where you're in someone's space awkwardly, I feel like just kept coming back, especially for Michael Scott.
但这种尴尬地侵入他人空间的肢体接触，我觉得一直都在出现，尤其是对迈克尔·斯科特来说。

1141
00:47:13.200 --> 00:47:18.580
Like he would talk to Jim and put his foot up on the desk, like basically lean in.
比如他会跟吉姆说话，然后把脚搁在桌子上，基本上就是凑过去。

1142
00:47:18.680 --> 00:47:20.900
So it's just like crotch facing you.
所以就是胯下对着你。

1143
00:47:21.220 --> 00:47:21.320
Yeah.
是啊。

1144
00:47:21.320 --> 00:47:23.860
And there are a lot of moments like that.
有很多这样的时刻。

1145
00:47:25.260 --> 00:47:30.620
I love those things, though, and especially when, if they're not in the script and you're not expecting them at all.
但我很喜欢这些时刻，尤其是当它们不在剧本里，而你完全没预料到的时候。

1146
00:47:30.780 --> 00:47:30.940
Yeah.
是啊。

1147
00:47:31.060 --> 00:47:41.300
I mean, obviously this brie scene was scripted, so I knew what the script was and the lines were, but I just didn't plan on having Ricky's crotch quite so clear to my brie.
我的意思是，显然这场布里干酪的戏是有剧本的，所以我知道剧本内容和台词，但我没料到瑞奇的胯下会离我的布里干酪那么近。

1148
00:47:43.400 --> 00:47:48.420
I didn't even count for that one ball to be so close to your sandwich.
我甚至没算到那颗蛋蛋会离你的三明治那么近。

1149
00:47:50.480 --> 00:47:59.300
Speaking of not being able to swallow your brie and breaking, you know, we broke all the time, but there were a few people that broke the moSt.
说到咽不下布里干酪和笑场，你知道，我们总是笑场，但有几个人笑场最多。

1150
00:47:59.560 --> 00:48:01.980
Like Rainn Wilson cracks himself up.
比如雷恩·威尔森就老是把自己逗笑。

1151
00:48:04.240 --> 00:48:06.380
He broke as Dwight a lot.
他演德怀特的时候经常笑场。

1152
00:48:07.280 --> 00:48:10.240
Mindy broke in almost every scene.
明迪几乎在每一场戏里都会笑场。

1153
00:48:11.080 --> 00:48:18.360
I remember Mindy, the character, doing the cabbage soup diet and looking awful.
我记得明迪那个角色当时在喝卷心菜汤减肥，看起来气色糟透了。

1154
00:48:18.520 --> 00:48:26.100
And I will do this now and I'll know if someone watches your show well, because she'll go, you're going to look amazing.
我现在就做这件事，如果有人看你的节目，我就会知道，因为她会说，你看起来棒极了。

1155
00:48:28.260 --> 00:48:29.460
I love it.
我喜欢这个。

1156
00:48:29.720 --> 00:48:31.060
Okay, so Mindy cracks up a lot.
好的，明迪经常笑个不停。

1157
00:48:31.180 --> 00:48:31.760
Yes, yes.
是，是。

1158
00:48:31.960 --> 00:48:37.820
But so on your set, now we know you had to exit a scene, but was there someone that broke the most?
但在你们的片场，我们知道你必须中途离场，但有没有人最容易笑场？

1159
00:48:39.480 --> 00:48:40.480
Was it Ricky?
是瑞奇吗？

1160
00:48:40.780 --> 00:48:48.520
Probably Ricky, but he broke more because he would see us breaking or trying not to.
大概是瑞奇，但他笑场更多是因为他看到我们在笑，或者在努力憋笑。

1161
00:48:49.380 --> 00:48:55.920
There was a scene, I think you might have seen it in bloopers, where Ricky and Martin are doing a scene.
有一场戏，我想你可能在花絮里看过，就是瑞奇和马丁演的那场。

1162
00:48:56.080 --> 00:48:58.700
It's the job evaluation scene.
就是工作评估那场戏。

1163
00:48:58.700 --> 00:49:07.060
And I came in to do my job evaluation scene and they were already nowhere near finished.
我进来准备拍工作评估那场戏时，他们离拍完还差得远呢。

1164
00:49:07.580 --> 00:49:14.060
And so we went over and over to lunch and then had to go back to it over lunch.
所以我们一直拍到午饭时间，午饭时还得接着拍。

1165
00:49:14.140 --> 00:49:17.460
And so we, because they couldn't, they couldn't get through it.
因为他们实在拍不完，所以我们就……

1166
00:49:17.600 --> 00:49:21.560
I saw that blooper and they keep like clacking the clacker.
我看了那个花絮，他们一直在打板。

1167
00:49:21.560 --> 00:49:24.760
And it was like upwards of like 30 takes.
大概拍了有30多条吧。

1168
00:49:25.020 --> 00:49:25.720
Oh my goodness.
天哪。

1169
00:49:26.400 --> 00:49:26.620
Yes.
是啊。

1170
00:49:26.620 --> 00:49:26.940
Yes.
没错。

1171
00:49:27.060 --> 00:49:34.200
And there was this moment that I remember from watching the show that was breaking them up.
我看剧的时候记得有个瞬间让他们笑场了。

1172
00:49:34.420 --> 00:49:35.720
And it's so funny.
真的太搞笑了。

1173
00:49:35.880 --> 00:49:43.720
It's just a gesture that where Ricky is saying like, you know, if you play your cards right, someday you might be in this chair.
那只是个动作，瑞奇当时说，你知道，如果你表现得好，总有一天你也能坐上这把椅子。

1174
00:49:44.020 --> 00:49:45.040
You might be in, yeah.
你可能也会坐在这儿，对。

1175
00:49:45.120 --> 00:49:49.720
And he does this like point down to his seat and he like bites his lip.
然后他指了指自己的座位，还咬了咬嘴唇。

1176
00:49:49.720 --> 00:49:50.640
He's like, yeah.
他当时就说，是啊。

1177
00:49:52.300 --> 00:49:54.960
And the first time he did it, they both broke.
他第一次演的时候，两人都笑场了。

1178
00:49:55.060 --> 00:49:56.600
And they're like, no, no, no, we got to get that.
他们就说，不行不行，我们得把这段拍下来。

1179
00:49:56.700 --> 00:49:57.240
We got to get that.
一定要拍下来。

1180
00:49:57.360 --> 00:49:57.860
Do that again.
再来一次。

1181
00:49:58.000 --> 00:49:58.420
Do that again.
再来一次。

1182
00:49:58.580 --> 00:50:01.020
But they never, I don't know how they ever got through it.
但他们从来没能忍住，我不知道他们是怎么演完的。

1183
00:50:01.300 --> 00:50:03.100
It was, but it was so funny.
确实，但真的太搞笑了。

1184
00:50:03.520 --> 00:50:09.840
I remember doing a scene later where Ricky is playing the guitar for me.
我记得后来拍了一场戏，瑞奇在给我弹吉他。

1185
00:50:09.960 --> 00:50:10.180
Yes.
对。

1186
00:50:10.180 --> 00:50:11.160
In his office.
在他的办公室里。

1187
00:50:11.520 --> 00:50:11.680
Yes.
对。

1188
00:50:11.740 --> 00:50:12.460
It's so funny.
太搞笑了。

1189
00:50:12.720 --> 00:50:13.660
It really is.
确实是。

1190
00:50:13.780 --> 00:50:14.980
And that, that was hard.
那场戏，那场戏很难演。

1191
00:50:14.980 --> 00:50:23.420
Um, I had written a song, my God, when I was 15, where I played the piano and sang this song.
嗯，我15岁时写过一首歌，天哪，当时我一边弹钢琴一边唱这首歌。

1192
00:50:23.560 --> 00:50:29.120
It was for my GCSE music, which is, I don't know, whatever exams you take here when you're 16.
那是为了我的GCSE音乐考试，就是你们这儿16岁时考的那种试，我也不清楚。

1193
00:50:30.000 --> 00:50:34.460
And, um, I got an A for my music.
然后，嗯，我的音乐课拿了A。

1194
00:50:34.640 --> 00:50:35.740
It's the only thing I ever got an A in.
那是我唯一拿过A的一门课。

1195
00:50:35.740 --> 00:50:48.320
And it was so bad because it was also kind of good, but it was a really cheery ditty that I was like, da, da, da, da, da, da.
那首歌真的很烂，但又有点好听，是一首特别欢快的小调，我就在那儿哒哒哒哒哒哒地唱。

1196
00:50:48.560 --> 00:50:53.000
And yet it was about the most horrific things, paedophiles.
但歌词写的却是最可怕的事情，关于恋童癖的。

1197
00:50:53.300 --> 00:50:53.700
Oh no.
噢，天哪。

1198
00:50:53.960 --> 00:51:03.440
And, and I'm not religious at all, but in the, in the chorus, it would be like, at the end of the worry and terror, there's heaven not far away.
而且，我一点也不信教，但在副歌里，我写的是，在忧虑和恐惧的尽头，天堂就在不远方。

1199
00:51:03.940 --> 00:51:08.640
And I remember telling Ricky and Steve this, and they were like, we have to have this in our show.
我记得我把这事告诉了瑞奇和史蒂夫，他们就说，我们一定要把它放进剧里。

1200
00:51:09.320 --> 00:51:13.760
And they worked their asses off in season two to try and get it in.
于是他们在第二季里拼了命地想把它加进去。

1201
00:51:14.020 --> 00:51:17.040
I couldn't, couldn't find a way to legitimately get it in.
我没法，没法找到合法的途径把它弄进去。

1202
00:51:17.300 --> 00:51:18.880
It was so bad.
那真是太烂了。

1203
00:51:19.060 --> 00:51:21.400
And it was so good because it was so bad.
但它又因为太烂而显得格外精彩。

1204
00:51:21.580 --> 00:51:22.800
It was crap plastic.
那是劣质塑料做的。

1205
00:51:23.240 --> 00:51:29.240
This was, I feel like this story is why you were destined to be cast on this show.
我觉得这个故事就是你注定要出演这部剧的原因。

1206
00:51:29.240 --> 00:51:32.700
Because your senses of humor were so aligned.
因为你们的幽默感太契合了。

1207
00:51:33.160 --> 00:51:41.860
This idea of like a song about all the things you kind of aren't supposed to say or discuss.
这个想法就像是一首关于那些你不该说或不该讨论的事情的歌。

1208
00:51:42.100 --> 00:51:42.280
Yeah.
没错。

1209
00:51:42.400 --> 00:51:43.240
In a peppy manner.
以一种活泼的方式。

1210
00:51:43.540 --> 00:51:44.620
In like a peppy show tune.
就像一首活泼的百老汇风格歌曲。

1211
00:51:44.640 --> 00:51:46.140
Never entered my head at 15.
我15岁时从未想过这些。

1212
00:51:46.400 --> 00:51:49.780
It was like a peppy show tune that could have opened a sitcom.
它就像一首可以作为情景喜剧开场曲的活泼乐曲。

1213
00:51:50.140 --> 00:51:50.520
Yes.
是的。

1214
00:51:50.900 --> 00:51:51.300
And.
而且。

1215
00:51:51.500 --> 00:51:52.860
About the darkest stuff.
关于最黑暗的事情。

1216
00:51:53.040 --> 00:51:53.260
Yeah.
没错。

1217
00:51:53.420 --> 00:51:54.440
About the darkest stuff.
关于最黑暗的事情。

1218
00:51:54.440 --> 00:51:56.360
Not, not religious at all.
一点也不，完全不涉及宗教。

1219
00:51:56.920 --> 00:52:01.900
And I went, Isaiah and Micah prophesied a friendly world of peace.
然后我说，以赛亚和弥迦预言了一个友好的和平世界。

1220
00:52:02.400 --> 00:52:02.700
What?
什么？

1221
00:52:03.480 --> 00:52:04.080
Did they?
他们预言了吗？

1222
00:52:04.380 --> 00:52:05.300
I have no idea.
我完全不知道。

1223
00:52:05.480 --> 00:52:06.200
But you got an A.
但你拿了个A。

1224
00:52:06.440 --> 00:52:07.280
I got an A.
我拿了个A。

1225
00:52:07.340 --> 00:52:07.960
You got an A.
你拿了个A。

1226
00:52:08.180 --> 00:52:09.400
So bar was low.
所以标准很低。

1227
00:52:12.020 --> 00:52:14.780
They might have just been in shock, didn't know what to make of it.
他们可能只是惊呆了，不知道该怎么评价。

1228
00:52:14.820 --> 00:52:16.820
I think it was like, poor girl.
我觉得他们当时想的是，可怜的女孩。

1229
00:52:17.020 --> 00:52:18.700
She's going nowhere in life.
她这辈子没戏了。

1230
00:52:18.800 --> 00:52:19.540
Let's give us something.
给她个及格吧。

1231
00:52:21.500 --> 00:52:22.580
All right.
好吧。

1232
00:52:22.680 --> 00:52:24.220
There's going to be a conference room meeting.
马上要开会议室会议了。

1233
00:52:24.480 --> 00:52:27.140
We have to discuss conference room scenes with you.
我们得和你讨论一下会议室的场景。

1234
00:52:27.400 --> 00:52:32.960
David Brent is going to discuss these rumors of downsizing.
大卫·布伦特要讨论关于裁员的传闻了。

1235
00:52:34.280 --> 00:52:36.780
How was this to shoot?
拍摄这段戏感觉如何？

1236
00:52:37.140 --> 00:52:37.440
Okay.
还可以。

1237
00:52:38.820 --> 00:52:42.300
Probably very like your conference scenes, which they take a long time.
可能很像你们的会议场景，非常耗时。

1238
00:52:42.480 --> 00:52:42.600
Yeah.
没错。

1239
00:52:43.280 --> 00:52:47.020
And at first you are genuinely trying to like be professional.
起初你确实在努力表现得专业。

1240
00:52:47.400 --> 00:52:48.660
Let's get it done, guys.
大家快点搞定吧。

1241
00:52:48.820 --> 00:52:49.160
Come on.
拜托。

1242
00:52:49.160 --> 00:52:49.800
Do you know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

1243
00:52:50.080 --> 00:52:50.780
This is fine.
这没问题。

1244
00:52:51.320 --> 00:52:56.680
And then, of course, as Rick is doing his speech and all of this, he'll change his speech.
然后，当然，当瑞克在做演讲时，他会不断修改他的演讲内容。

1245
00:52:57.120 --> 00:52:58.920
And so you're listening.
所以你得听着。

1246
00:52:58.940 --> 00:52:59.980
And so you're doing it.
所以你得照做。

1247
00:53:00.340 --> 00:53:01.740
And then I have one bit more.
然后我还有一点要补充。

1248
00:53:02.740 --> 00:53:07.640
I was doing, I had a line, something like, well, Jennifer, so I say something like, well,
我当时在演，我有一句台词，大概是，嗯，詹妮弗，所以我说类似，嗯，

1249
00:53:07.920 --> 00:53:11.060
Jennifer said there might be some job losses or downsizing.
詹妮弗说可能会有一些裁员或缩减规模的情况。

1250
00:53:11.220 --> 00:53:11.420
Yes.
是的。

1251
00:53:11.680 --> 00:53:12.140
Or something.
或者类似的话。

1252
00:53:12.300 --> 00:53:14.960
He calls on you hoping that you're going to save the day.
他找你是希望你能力挽狂澜。

1253
00:53:15.200 --> 00:53:17.280
But he said you like make it worse.
但他却说你反而把事情搞砸了。

1254
00:53:17.280 --> 00:53:23.100
And Ricky was sitting and Steve was sitting at the monitors for me doing this line.
当时瑞奇和史蒂夫坐在监视器前，让我演这句台词。

1255
00:53:24.060 --> 00:53:25.360
And I did it.
我演了。

1256
00:53:25.520 --> 00:53:28.960
The note was a little less soap opera loose.
他们给的建议是让我别演得那么像肥皂剧。

1257
00:53:28.960 --> 00:53:31.320
And I went, oh, okay.
我心想，哦，好吧。

1258
00:53:31.700 --> 00:53:35.480
I think because I had this one line in this long scene, I think I might have been trying
我想是因为在那场长戏里我只有这一句台词，我可能想

1259
00:53:35.480 --> 00:53:38.600
to really make it last a while.
让它显得更有分量一点。

1260
00:53:42.560 --> 00:53:44.580
Yeah, so I made it less soapy.
没错，所以我演得没那么像肥皂剧了。

1261
00:53:45.960 --> 00:53:47.820
That made me just have a question.
这让我产生了一个疑问。

1262
00:53:48.100 --> 00:53:51.600
So was he the one usually yelling things off camera to you guys?
所以通常是他在镜头外对你们大喊大叫吗？

1263
00:53:51.740 --> 00:53:56.960
Was he, they co-directed, but was Stephen Merchant more the one sort of like yelling action,
他们是联合导演，但史蒂芬·莫昌特是不是更多负责喊“开始”，

1264
00:53:57.120 --> 00:53:58.560
giving notes and stuff like that?
给建议之类的？

1265
00:53:58.680 --> 00:54:01.100
Yeah, I think Steve would have done action more.
是的，我觉得史蒂夫更多负责喊“开始”。

1266
00:54:01.100 --> 00:54:05.220
Or our first AD, more so if Rick is in the scene.
或者如果瑞奇在戏里的话，就是我们的第一副导演负责。

1267
00:54:05.360 --> 00:54:10.120
If he's not in the scene, he's usually changed back into his sweats and chomping on a sandwich,
如果他不在戏里，他通常会换回运动服，一边啃着三明治，

1268
00:54:10.620 --> 00:54:11.880
watching the monitor.
一边看着监视器。

1269
00:54:14.120 --> 00:54:17.180
But yeah, so that would be Steve normally.
但没错，通常都是史蒂夫负责。

1270
00:54:17.660 --> 00:54:18.920
Yeah, that makes sense.
嗯，这说得通。

1271
00:54:19.060 --> 00:54:19.520
I mean, because...
我是说，因为……

1272
00:54:19.520 --> 00:54:24.460
It would be kind of fun, like co-directing and acting in the thing that you've written.
一边联合导演，一边在自己写的剧本里演戏，感觉挺有趣的。

1273
00:54:24.860 --> 00:54:25.340
Yeah.
是啊。

1274
00:54:25.480 --> 00:54:26.220
That's really cool.
那真的很酷。

1275
